    │   Any change must not alter the on-wire CRC value or existing RTU/Modbus telemetry
    │   frames become unverifiable
    └── The file uses zlib.crc32 purely as a CRC-32 checksum function over byte 
        payloads. The module's own docstring identifies fastcrc as the intended drop-in 
        substitution target for this exact use case, and fastcrc exposes a compatible 
        crc32() function returning the same standard CRC-32 (IEEE 802.3) checksum, 
        making it a genuine like-for-like replacement for this narrow usage.

