  ⚠ Remaining incompatibilities noted by connector LLM:
    - ujson.dumps has no 'separators' parameter; a wrapper can strip it and post-process
whitespace but this is a workaround, not a native equivalent, so behavior parity relies 
on ujson's default compact formatting remaining stable across versions.
    - ujson's float formatting/precision can differ from stdlib json's repr-based float 
serialization; no wrapper can guarantee byte-for-byte determinism for arbitrary float 
values without re-implementing json's own float-to-string algorithm, which undermines 
the point of migrating to ujson for a hard determinism requirement.
    - ujson has historically inconsistent/incomplete spec compliance for NaN/Infinity 
handling and unicode escaping compared to stdlib json; if any sensor value or tag ever 
contains such edge-case content, audit log output could silently diverge from the 
deterministic format required, and this is a core behavioral gap in the serialization 
engine itself, not a simple call-site mismatch fixable by a thin wrapper.

