  ⚠ Remaining incompatibilities noted by connector LLM:
    - paho's synchronous connect()-then-reuse client lifecycle (client.connect(host, 
port) in _default_client) has no equivalent in aiomqtt; aiomqtt only connects via 'async
with Client(...) as client', which is an async context manager, not a method callable on
an already-constructed object outside async code.
    - TelemetryBridge.publish_reading and publish_batch are defined as plain synchronous
methods that call self.client.publish(...) and read a return value's .rc attribute. 
aiomqtt.Client.publish is a coroutine that must be awaited inside an active async 
context; no wrapper can convert a sync method into an async one without changing every 
caller of TelemetryBridge to async/await, which is outside the scope of glue code around
a single call site.
    - The dependency-injection pattern (client passed into TelemetryBridge.__init__ and 
reused across many publish calls) assumes a persistent, already-connected client object 
usable outside of any context manager scope; aiomqtt's connection object is only valid 
within its 'async with' block, so the injected client's usable lifetime does not match 
how TelemetryBridge holds and reuses self.client.
    - info.rc extraction (getattr(info, 'rc', 0)) depends on paho's MessageInfo return 
value; aiomqtt.publish returns None on success and raises on failure, meaning the whole 
error-handling/telemetry-result contract of publish_reading must be redesigned 
(try/except plus manual rc synthesis), which is a change to the code's execution/error 
model rather than a pure glue wrapper.

