Equivalence Groups Found
└── MQTT client for publishing telemetry to a broker
    ├── Candidates : paho.mqtt.client, gmqtt, amqtt
    ├── Used APIs  : mqtt.Client, client.connect, client.publish
    ├── Pitfalls   : paho-mqtt is synchronous/callback-based; gmqtt and amqtt are 
    │   asyncio-based, requiring the calling code (publish_reading, publish_batch, 
    │   _default_client) to become async; Connection semantics differ: paho uses 
    │   connect() + loop management, gmqtt/amqtt use async context managers or explicit 
    │   event loop integration; publish() return value differs: paho returns a 
    │   MessageInfo object with .rc, async libraries return coroutines or None, breaking
    │   the getattr(info, 'rc', 0) pattern; hbmqtt (an often-suggested alternative) is 
    │   deprecated in favor of amqtt and should be avoided for new code; QoS handling 
    │   and client_id semantics may differ slightly between libraries
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── paho-mqtt's Client is used synchronously to connect and publish sensor readings 
        to an MQTT broker. gmqtt and amqtt are both actively maintained MQTT client 
        libraries that could serve the same broker-publishing role. They are 
        functionally equivalent at the protocol level (MQTT pub/sub) and could 
        substitute for paho-mqtt as the underlying transport for TelemetryBridge.

