Equivalence Groups Found
└── email/notification sending backend
    ├── Candidates : smtplib, apprise
    ├── Used APIs  : SMTP, sendmail
    ├── Pitfalls   : apprise's API is notify(title, body) rather than sendmail(sender, 
    │   recipients, message) - call sites need to be rewritten, not just the import; 
    │   apprise manages its own service URLs/config for recipients instead of raw SMTP 
    │   host/port/credentials; smtplib is synchronous and blocking; apprise may dispatch
    │   some notification types asynchronously depending on plugin; error handling 
    │   differs: smtplib raises SMTPException subclasses, apprise typically returns a 
    │   boolean success/failure; the dependency-injected `smtp` object in EmailNotifier 
    │   expects a `.sendmail()` method, so a connector/shim is needed to expose an 
    │   SMTP-compatible interface backed by apprise
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file's own docstring explicitly identifies apprise as the intended 
        substitution target for smtplib-based email notification. Both smtplib (via 
        SMTP().sendmail) and apprise (via .notify()) can deliver an alert message to a 
        recipient, making them functionally equivalent for the 'send an operator 
        notification' role even though apprise supports many more transport backends 
        beyond raw SMTP.

