│   10     """Bridge smtplib.SMTP's connect/sendmail interface onto apprise.           │
│   11                                                                                 │
│   12     smtplib.SMTP(host, port) returns a live connection object whose             │
│   13     .sendmail(sender, recipients, message) method ships a raw RFC822            │
│   14     message over the wire, returning None on success and raising an             │
│   15     smtplib.SMTPException subclass on failure.                                  │
│   16                                                                                 │
│   17     apprise has no concept of a persistent SMTP connection or a raw             │
│   18     RFC822 message. Instead, an apprise.Apprise() instance is configured        │
│   19     with one or more service URLs (here, a mailto:// URL built from the         │
│   20     host/port/recipients), and delivery happens via a single synchronous        │
│   21     call: apprise_obj.notify(title=..., body=...), which returns True/False     │
│   22     instead of raising for ordinary delivery failures.                          │
│   23                                                                                 │
│   24     This wrapper returns a small shim object exposing an SMTP-compatible        │
│   25     .sendmail(sender, recipients, message) method. That method: builds an       │
│   26     Apprise() instance pointed at a mailto:// URL derived from host/port        │
│   27     and the recipient list, naively parses the RFC822-style `message`           │
│   28     string to pull out the "Subject:" header and split it from the body,        │
│   29     forwards those to notify(title=subject, body=body), and converts a          │
│   30     False return into a raised exception that mimics                            │
│   31     smtplib.SMTPException, so existing callers such as                          │
│   32     `self.smtp.sendmail(...)` keep working without modification.                │
│   33     """                                                                         │
