  ⚠ Remaining incompatibilities noted by connector LLM:
    - amqtt's client API (connect/publish/disconnect) is exclusively coroutine-based and
requires an asyncio event loop; paho-mqtt's synchronous MqttSink.publish()->int contract
cannot be preserved without turning MqttSink and all its callers into async code 
(await-based), which is a structural redesign, not something a call-site wrapper can 
transparently fix.
    - amqtt is designed around 'async with Client() as client' context-manager lifecycle
management for connect/disconnect; the current _default_client()/MqttSink design assumes
a persistent, eagerly-connected synchronous client object with no async context, so the 
connection lifecycle model itself must be restructured.
    - Even with sync-over-async bridging wrappers (e.g. asyncio.run per call), this 
breaks if MqttSink.publish() is ever called from within an already-running event loop 
(e.g. if the host application is itself async), which is a common real-world constraint 
