    │   significantly (context managers vs explicit connect/disconnect calls); QoS, 
    │   reconnect, and callback registration APIs differ across these libraries
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── paho-mqtt is used here as a synchronous, callback-based MQTT client to connect 
        and publish messages. gmqtt, amqtt, and aiomqtt are all MQTT client libraries 
        that could serve the same functional role (connecting to a broker and publishing
        messages), making them plausible substitutes for the broker-communication task. 
        However, they are async-first (asyncio-based context managers/coroutines) while 
        paho-mqtt is sync/callback-based, so a direct drop-in replacement is not 
        possible without wrapping async calls or restructuring the calling code.

