exactly the kind of fundamentally different async/sync execution model that a wrapper 
cannot transparently fix, as noted in the migration pitfalls.
    - The current design stores a long-lived `self.client` object and calls plain 
methods on it synchronously; aiomqtt has no supported pattern for holding a connected 
client outside of an active `async with` block, so persistent client reuse across 
multiple publish() calls (as done in _default_client/MqttSink) cannot be preserved 
without restructuring the whole application's control flow to async.

